WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:11.269
Hi, welcome back to our at-home retreat.

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:18.720
I'd like to thank Stanley Chen for

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:20.189
coming to translate. He and Alison have

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:25.650
been working very hard, and thank you for

00:00:20.189 --> 00:00:32.790
that. Session 19, we call it "One Wheel,

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:36.690
Three Lives." And the picture you see

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:47.489
here is of three sets of twelve

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:53.969
links, like in three wheels. And the image

00:00:47.489 --> 00:00:57.469
I want you to have in your mind, is the

00:00:53.969 --> 00:01:02.640
links of the first wheel start to turn,

00:00:57.469 --> 00:01:08.159
and then before it finishes, it triggers

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:12.869
another wheel, and then before that

00:01:08.159 --> 00:01:16.100
finishes, it triggers another wheel. So

00:01:12.869 --> 00:01:21.900
before the first wheel is finished,

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:27.150
there's a second wheel started. And is it

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:34.790
possible a third wheel starts? Because if

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:34.790
that's true, the things we do in one day,

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:47.790
they might interact for thousands of

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:50.600
lives. We could be creating thousands of

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:50.600
lives in one day.

00:01:53.100 --> 00:02:03.009
Then don't forget what our big job is in

00:01:56.740 --> 00:02:08.890
the lam rim (LAM RIM), in this middle

00:02:03.009 --> 00:02:13.170
motivation person--they're trying to

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:17.319
reach Nirvana, just for themselves.

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:19.000
They're trying to stop the Wheel of Life,

00:02:17.319 --> 00:02:20.680
which also you can call "wheel of

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:32.140
pain." It's not a wheel of life; it's a

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:34.930
wheel of pain. So it's okay if you want to

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:36.459
think of one wheel with twelve parts, and

00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:45.730
you have to stop it. You can think like

00:02:36.459 --> 00:02:50.980
that. But at some point, you're going to

00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:52.840
have to realize that in one day you are

00:02:50.980 --> 00:03:04.450
triggering hundreds of thousands of

00:02:52.840 --> 00:03:10.840
wheels--lifetimes. But there are also many

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:13.019
wheels going on. Like the wife in the

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:13.019
kitchen,

00:03:13.739 --> 00:03:25.389
last week she yelled at her kids. She

00:03:18.549 --> 00:03:35.349
started a mini wheel going. She did

00:03:25.389 --> 00:03:37.359
link one, and two, and half of three--and

00:03:35.349 --> 00:03:44.829
then that triggered things in the

00:03:37.359 --> 00:03:47.349
kitchen, three or four days later. The

00:03:44.829 --> 00:03:55.690
husband yelled at her before she had

00:03:47.349 --> 00:03:59.280
a chance to talk. Then she says, "He yells

00:03:55.690 --> 00:03:59.280
at me. I didn't even say anything yet!"

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:08.820
Then she yells back. And it's amazing

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:20.670
that in, I don't know, a hundred thousand

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:22.110
years people didn't figure it out. They

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:31.050
didn't figure out that the husband is

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:33.480
yelling because the you yelled at your kids last week. And

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:36.180
they didn't figure out that if you yell

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:45.180
at your husband, then the kids are going to

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:48.630
be bad next week. Then you're gonna yell

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:51.360
at your kids again. See, you get this

00:04:48.630 --> 00:05:00.060
feeling that multiple wheels are being set in

00:04:51.360 --> 00:05:05.430
motion. In the example we just gave, there's

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:13.260
three lifetimes already. Kids bedroom, Friday

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:18.540
night. Kitchen the next Wednesday. Kids

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:23.160
bedroom next ... the week after that.

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:28.440
Wheels within wheels. So this ...

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:32.040
today's discussion, session 19, let's look

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:35.720
at three lifetimes in a single set of

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:35.720
twelve links. We're not going to call it one wheel, maybe.

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:49.370
de na le chig gi wang du chepay tendrel cha tsang...
(DES NA LAS GCIG GI DBANG DU BYAS PA'I RTEN CHA TSANG...)

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:52.729
...chig tse chig la dzok mi si
(...GCIG TSE GCIG LA RDZOGS MI SRID)
Here's a

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:58.490
very, I don't know, controversial

00:05:52.729 --> 00:06:01.669
statement. If you're talking with

00:05:58.490 --> 00:06:14.030
reference to--wang du che (DBANG DU BYAS)--if you're talking

00:06:01.669 --> 00:06:18.560
with reference to one karmic seed, then it's

00:06:14.030 --> 00:06:22.039
impossible for a whole wheel to finish

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:24.740
in one life. We'd like to think one wheel

00:06:22.039 --> 00:06:48.440
is one life, but it's actually impossible

00:06:24.740 --> 00:06:49.849
to finish a whole wheel in one life. If you didn't

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:51.319
get that right away, then just think

00:06:49.849 --> 00:06:53.840
about it. I mean sometimes you should

00:06:51.319 --> 00:06:56.270
stop listening to the video, go sit on

00:06:53.840 --> 00:07:11.569
your couch, and just think about it for

00:06:56.270 --> 00:07:17.090
ten minutes. In a traditional Buddhist class in

00:07:11.569 --> 00:07:23.029
the monastery, you're absolutely not

00:07:17.090 --> 00:07:27.259
allowed to drink anything, obviously not

00:07:23.029 --> 00:07:32.210
allowed to eat anything, not allowed to

00:07:27.259 --> 00:07:37.729
go peepee even. Sometimes the class is three

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:40.479
hours! And this video system is so cool

00:07:37.729 --> 00:07:40.479
for you.

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:49.660
I mean you can even sit on a toilet and

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:56.500
watch this, and eat pizza at the same

00:07:49.660 --> 00:07:59.530
time. Okay, so I don't recommend. Okay

00:07:56.500 --> 00:08:03.460
gyog kyang tse nyi ni ngepar gu la
(MGYOGS KYANG TSE GNYIS NI NGES PAR DGOS LA)

00:07:59.530 --> 00:08:07.090
So therefore, logically, we just found out

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:11.200
that even at the fastest, it's going to

00:08:07.090 --> 00:08:13.270
take two lives to make the seed, water

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:31.150
the seed, and have the seed open into a

00:08:13.270 --> 00:08:37.300
life. So just get in this mood of a

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:41.229
seed is planted, and then there's another

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:48.820
series of events which make it ready to

00:08:41.229 --> 00:08:57.640
open--which water it. And then, thirdly, it

00:08:48.820 --> 00:08:59.290
opens into, for example, a new life.
yang le la... (YANG LAS LA...)

00:08:57.640 --> 00:09:02.800
...se len gyi su tab...
(...SRED LEN GYIS GSOS BTAB...)

00:08:59.290 --> 00:09:11.650
...ma nupar gyang na
(...MA NUS PAR 'GYANGS NA)
Now what happens if the

00:09:02.800 --> 00:09:13.420
seed doesn't get water or fertilizer? And

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:17.050
I'm trying to remember the name of that

00:09:13.420 --> 00:09:19.620
Siberian plant, but it's ... I'll give it to

00:09:17.050 --> 00:09:19.620
you tomorrow.

00:09:22.499 --> 00:09:33.039
But what if that seed drops into a

00:09:26.589 --> 00:09:37.619
glacier and it doesn't get real water or

00:09:33.039 --> 00:09:37.619
sunlight for thirty-one thousand years?

00:09:42.539 --> 00:09:49.419
What happens then?

00:09:45.869 --> 00:09:54.429
Okay, so he gives he gives a... what do

00:09:49.419 --> 00:10:02.729
call it? A scenario. 
pen je kyi yenlak sum...
('PHEN BYED KYI YAN LAG GSUM...)

00:09:54.429 --> 00:10:02.740
...tse chig la
(...TSE GCIG LA)

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:11.439
The throwing links--the misunderstanding your husband. Talking,

00:10:07.299 --> 00:10:15.639
saying something bad to him, and planting

00:10:11.439 --> 00:10:21.879
the seed on your mind. Let's say those

00:10:15.639 --> 00:10:24.459
are finished in the first life, then it

00:10:21.879 --> 00:10:27.759
doesn't happen that those seeds get

00:10:24.459 --> 00:10:31.419
water or fertilizer before that lady

00:10:27.759 --> 00:10:42.609
dies. What if she dies, I don't know, that

00:10:31.419 --> 00:10:47.439
night? Then she's going to be carrying seeds

00:10:42.609 --> 00:10:56.889
to her next life, and then they're going to

00:10:47.439 --> 00:10:58.689
have to be watered in the second life. We

00:10:56.889 --> 00:11:01.929
call the factory seeds, right? Really they

00:10:58.689 --> 00:11:05.219
prepare the seed for opening, like

00:11:01.929 --> 00:11:05.219
building a new car.

00:11:13.550 --> 00:11:21.449
So she planted the seed in the first

00:11:15.990 --> 00:11:25.759
life, she died suddenly. In the second

00:11:21.449 --> 00:11:25.759
life, they got water and fertilizer,

00:11:27.679 --> 00:11:33.889
because that mind which went into the

00:11:31.319 --> 00:11:37.499
second life was still misunderstanding

00:11:33.889 --> 00:11:52.679
her bad seeds, which is the best water to

00:11:37.499 --> 00:11:54.149
make them strong. So, suppose those seeds

00:11:52.679 --> 00:12:03.209
get water, but then she dies again

00:11:54.149 --> 00:12:08.189
suddenly, before they can open. Then they

00:12:03.209 --> 00:12:11.040
will open in the third life. Okay? Those

00:12:08.189 --> 00:12:13.579
four seeds in the middle--four, five,

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:13.579
six, and seven--

00:12:16.189 --> 00:12:26.999
body and mind in the womb,

00:12:20.749 --> 00:12:31.470
sense organs developing, contact with the

00:12:26.999 --> 00:12:38.119
outside world, and a feeling about how

00:12:31.470 --> 00:12:44.809
that contact feels. Plus, eleven--

00:12:38.119 --> 00:12:49.369
whole rebirth experience. Plus, twelve--

00:12:44.809 --> 00:12:49.369
living a whole life and then dying again.

00:12:49.459 --> 00:12:53.569
Those are going to finish in the third life.

00:12:55.670 --> 00:13:01.529
Therefore we can say that it is possible

00:12:58.470 --> 00:13:04.529
that it can take three lives for one set

00:13:01.529 --> 00:13:07.369
of twelve, but it may not be consecutive

00:13:04.529 --> 00:13:07.369
wheels.

00:13:11.710 --> 00:13:22.420
Then he gives a real example. And

00:13:20.589 --> 00:13:25.330
there's a problem with the carving here

00:13:22.420 --> 00:13:30.190
that I think should be read

00:13:25.330 --> 00:13:31.930
differently. The yu de (YOD DE) I think

00:13:30.190 --> 00:13:35.880
should be read yu do (YOD DO), which makes

00:13:31.930 --> 00:13:35.880
more sense, and it's kind of important.

00:13:43.290 --> 00:13:51.370
Okay. de yang per na (DE YANG DPER NA)--
let's take a real

00:13:46.930 --> 00:13:55.270
example. 
tse dir ngen song gi las...
(TSE 'DIR NGAN SONG GI LAS...)

00:13:51.370 --> 00:13:57.610
...sag
(...BSAGS)--
in this lifetime you do some kind

00:13:55.270 --> 00:14:00.700
of action towards another person which

00:13:57.610 --> 00:14:04.050
is so bad you're going to become an animal,

00:14:00.700 --> 00:14:04.050
or go to hell, or something like that.

00:14:14.010 --> 00:14:30.250
le sag (LAS BSAGS) means that seed has been

00:14:17.490 --> 00:14:34.390
injected into the mind. kyang (KYANG).
I'm glad I didn't

00:14:30.250 --> 00:14:36.779
bet any money. chi kar ('CHI KHAR)--at the moment of

00:14:34.390 --> 00:14:36.779
your death,

00:14:37.290 --> 00:14:46.750
lama sog kyi ge sem la tsu
(BLA MA SOGS KYIS DGE SEMS LA BTZUD)

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:48.730
teacher, standing there, and they're like

00:14:46.750 --> 00:14:53.620
"Try to think of something good! Try

00:14:48.730 --> 00:14:56.440
to think of something good!" Then there's no

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:59.709
negative water, there's no negative fertilizer...

00:14:56.440 --> 00:15:01.959
there's nothing to trigger the bad

00:14:59.709 --> 00:15:03.579
karma at the moment that you die, because

00:15:01.959 --> 00:15:06.300
your lama was standing there telling you

00:15:03.579 --> 00:15:06.300
to have good thoughts.

00:15:15.750 --> 00:15:23.019
And by the way, that's a very practical

00:15:20.709 --> 00:15:33.610
reason why you should stay close to a

00:15:23.019 --> 00:15:35.589
lama. People ask me, "Well, in the

00:15:33.610 --> 00:15:38.019
modern world with the internet, then I

00:15:35.589 --> 00:15:50.980
don't really have to stay physically

00:15:38.019 --> 00:15:55.560
nearby my lama." But sometimes I get scared and I

00:15:50.980 --> 00:15:55.560
think I should always stay near my lama,

00:15:58.769 --> 00:16:03.850
because if I have a bad accident or

00:16:01.990 --> 00:16:07.649
something, they can they can reach me in

00:16:03.850 --> 00:16:07.649
ten or twenty minutes--that would be best, right?

00:16:14.880 --> 00:16:21.699
Okay.
mir kye gyur gyi le shik la su tab
(MIR SKYE 'GYUR GYI LAS SHIG LA GSOS BTAB)--

00:16:18.880 --> 00:16:24.610
because the lama was standing there and

00:16:21.699 --> 00:16:27.639
giving good advice at the moment of the

00:16:24.610 --> 00:16:32.430
selection of the karma for the next life,

00:16:27.639 --> 00:16:32.430
they were born as a human instead of a

00:16:47.939 --> 00:16:55.670
dog. So they're born as a human,

00:16:51.300 --> 00:17:01.500
and of course they're going to die again,

00:16:55.670 --> 00:17:10.319
but in this example they got angry in

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:12.270
the hospital at the last minute, and that

00:17:10.319 --> 00:17:19.230
put water and fertilizer on this

00:17:12.270 --> 00:17:23.220
negative seeds. And then the seed that was

00:17:19.230 --> 00:17:32.640
collected in the first life got watered

00:17:23.220 --> 00:17:42.450
in the second life, and then created the

00:17:32.640 --> 00:17:44.550
third life in the lower realms. 
de tsun ne (DES MTSON NAS)--So

00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:49.740
just taking that one example, we can

00:17:44.550 --> 00:17:51.750
understand 
pen je dang drup je kyi bar du
('PHEN BYED DANG 'GRUB BYED KYI BAR DU)--

00:17:49.740 --> 00:18:01.800
between the arrow shooting and the

00:17:51.750 --> 00:18:06.030
factory producing a new life,
tse du me...
(TSE DU MAS...)

00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:17.160
...chu
(...CHOD)--
there could be many intervening

00:18:06.030 --> 00:18:19.559
lifetimes where nothing happens. 
tendrel...
(RTEN 'BREL...)

00:18:17.160 --> 00:18:26.160
...shen gyi tse yin pe drang du mi dren
(...GZHAN GYI TSE YIN PAS GRANGS SU MI 'DREN)--

00:18:19.559 --> 00:18:32.610
now, let's say you did some really

00:18:26.160 --> 00:18:37.950
bad karma in the first life, then in the

00:18:32.610 --> 00:18:41.070
second life it didn't get water, and then

00:18:37.950 --> 00:18:46.410
in the third life you got water at the

00:18:41.070 --> 00:18:53.760
end of your life, and then it triggered a

00:18:46.410 --> 00:19:00.780
new life. Is it four wheel parts? Is it

00:18:53.760 --> 00:19:09.320
sections from four wheels? It's four

00:19:00.780 --> 00:19:16.050
lifetimes. The answer is, by tradition, we

00:19:09.320 --> 00:19:19.020
don't count this one. Why? Nothing

00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:25.320
happened. Nothing happened with this

00:19:19.020 --> 00:19:29.309
seed. I'll say it again. First life you

00:19:25.320 --> 00:19:33.620
do something really bad--you plant a bad

00:19:29.309 --> 00:19:36.280
seed, but it doesn't get watered by

00:19:33.620 --> 00:19:43.900
negative

00:19:36.280 --> 00:19:44.650
coffee meditation, for example. So in the

00:19:43.900 --> 00:19:46.150
second life,

00:19:44.650 --> 00:19:51.970
nothing happens with the seed--it's just

00:19:46.150 --> 00:19:56.049
sitting in your mind. In the third life,

00:19:51.970 --> 00:20:03.039
you feel happy about doing the

00:19:56.049 --> 00:20:05.230
same bad thing. That happiness about bad

00:20:03.039 --> 00:20:08.909
things in the third life puts water on

00:20:05.230 --> 00:20:08.909
the bad seed from the first life, and

00:20:14.250 --> 00:20:24.220
then the seed from the first life that

00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:29.200
got watered in the third life creates a

00:20:24.220 --> 00:20:35.919
bad rebirth in the fourth life. And by

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:37.809
tradition, in these Abhidharma teachings, when

00:20:35.919 --> 00:20:48.340
we say "how many lifetimes did it take

00:20:37.809 --> 00:20:52.500
the seed to do its thing," by tradition, we

00:20:48.340 --> 00:21:03.100
only consider these three to be one set--

00:20:52.500 --> 00:21:07.450
belong to the same set. So now I have

00:21:03.100 --> 00:21:12.520
another question for Stanley. Hundred

00:21:07.450 --> 00:21:19.000
dollars. If he wins, he's going to donate it to

00:21:12.520 --> 00:21:21.070
the Mixed Nuts translations. Is it

00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:24.240
possible to have more than three lives

00:21:21.070 --> 00:21:24.240
in a single set? Yes or no? 
[Stanley: In this tradition, no.]

00:21:33.080 --> 00:21:39.320
Good, okay. Hundred dollars. I owe a hundred dollars to the Mixed Nuts.

00:21:39.710 --> 00:21:47.100
Hopefully it'll be for refreshments,

00:21:42.750 --> 00:21:52.500
because I'll be there. Okay, so now we're

00:21:47.100 --> 00:21:56.490
going to wrap up.
dor na (MDOR NA) means okay "just

00:21:52.500 --> 00:21:59.550
to summarize"
tendrel tsar chik gi wang du... 
(RTEN 'BREL TSAR GCIG GI DBANG DU...)
 tend outside check you on

00:21:56.490 --> 00:22:06.030
...chepa
(...BYAS PA)--
if we restrict ourselves to one

00:21:59.550 --> 00:22:09.679
set of dependence, or dependent

00:22:06.030 --> 00:22:09.679
origination, which means one wheel,

00:22:11.610 --> 00:22:21.000
yenlak nam nyur na tse nyi
(YAN LAG RNAMS MYUR NA TSE GNYIS)--
at the

00:22:15.179 --> 00:22:23.429
fastest, it's going to take two lives.
yun ring...
(YUN RING...)

00:22:21.000 --> 00:22:29.330
...na tse sum
(...NA TSE GSUM)--
at the slowest, it's going to

00:22:23.429 --> 00:22:32.040
take three lives. 
de le nyur gyang mi si
(DE LAS MYUR 'GYANG MI SRID)--

00:22:29.330 --> 00:22:38.640
impossible to have less lives or more

00:22:32.040 --> 00:22:44.400
lives. And I have an image here at the

00:22:38.640 --> 00:23:01.050
end, which is many gears in a

00:22:44.400 --> 00:23:05.630
watch. I'm going to get it up here for Stanley. There you go. So

00:23:01.050 --> 00:23:07.950
this shows the inside of a watch. And

00:23:05.630 --> 00:23:09.240
different gears are connecting with

00:23:07.950 --> 00:23:19.290
different gears... they're all turning at the

00:23:09.240 --> 00:23:22.440
same time. And it means every moment of

00:23:19.290 --> 00:23:26.150
your life is interconnected with many

00:23:22.440 --> 00:23:26.150
past lives and many future lives.

00:23:32.950 --> 00:23:44.330
Then if you really understood these last

00:23:35.690 --> 00:23:46.900
three or four classes, you should be

00:23:44.330 --> 00:23:51.140
freaked out.

00:23:46.900 --> 00:23:53.330
"Oh, Geshe-la, if a thousand wheels are spinning

00:23:51.140 --> 00:24:02.020
at the same time, different

00:23:53.330 --> 00:24:06.650
sets, what am I supposed to do?

00:24:02.020 --> 00:24:07.960
What do you want me to do? How can I stop

00:24:06.650 --> 00:24:12.830
it?

00:24:07.960 --> 00:24:14.200
How can I get out of pain? How can I

00:24:12.830 --> 00:24:21.080
reach Nirvana?"

00:24:14.200 --> 00:24:25.580
The answer is marmahatha--
Strike

00:24:21.080 --> 00:24:28.760
at the killing point. Where's the weak

00:24:25.580 --> 00:24:34.130
point... I saw a movie the other

00:24:28.760 --> 00:24:40.610
